From: Dominggoes Isakh <drjisakh@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 20:36:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 14/17] Hide the whole camera2.legacy package from the public
 API

package.html's {@hide} is the old doclava convention and is no longer
honored by metalava; package-info.java with a @hide javadoc is the
convention this tree actually uses elsewhere (e.g.
com.android.internal). Without it, every restored legacy class (not
just CameraDeviceUserShim) was leaking into current.txt and other
tracked API-surface files as public SDK API, which is how the
MQDescriptor parsing failure and system_server stub-from-text failures
both arose. Regenerated current.txt accordingly, which now also drops
the earlier manual deletions as redundant with the full regeneration.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: Ia8cfd8a7586494d38b3fb248131724672e83fa76
